<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY THREE-MONTH BILL YIELD RISES TO 19.51 PCT.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY THREE-MONTH BILL YIELD RISES TO 19.51 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of three-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 19.51 percent, up from 19.49 percent at an auction one week ago, the Government Debt Management Agency said.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     14,760.48 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    19.51 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     95.4101 pct</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
